{"nodes": [{"id": "brain_log_63_r4_metric_ordering_result_r4_metric_ordering", "label": "R4 \u2014 does the headline metric change the ladder's decision?", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "brain/log/63_R4_metric_ordering_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Supplies the measurement gate G1 should rest on; explicitly does not decide it."}, {"id": "brain_log_63_r4_metric_ordering_result_eval_metric_ordering", "label": "eval/metric_ordering.py (new module)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/log/63_R4_metric_ordering_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No refits: committed per-fold loss vectors are re-read and the same MCS instrument re-run under each loss."}, {"id": "brain_log_63_r4_metric_ordering_result_argmin_metric_dependence", "label": "The argmin is metric-dependent at every scaled venue", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/log/63_R4_metric_ordering_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kolassa's objection is not abstract here: the winner changes under MASE vs RMSSE at both scaled venues, so a bare argmin would ship a different model."}, {"id": "brain_log_63_r4_metric_ordering_result_mcs_metric_invariance", "label": "The model confidence set is metric-invariant", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/log/63_R4_metric_ordering_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The set of models the data cannot separate is identical under either loss at both venues, which is why the strong defence is that no conclusion rests on a ranking."}, {"id": "brain_log_63_r4_metric_ordering_result_beer_hall_coin_toss", "label": "Beer Hall flip is a coin-toss (gap 0.0001-0.0002)", "fil